   "etymology": "From mbanj (Arbëreshë), from *ënbanj (compare Old Gheg ënbaj), the *m- being from Proto-Albanian *en- (intensive prefix). The identity of the root is disputed.\n* Orel posits Proto-Albanian *barnja, a causative formed to Proto-Indo-European *bʰer- (“to carry”).\n* Schumacher and DPEWA after him insist on a derivation from Proto-Indo-European *peh₂- (“to protect”).",
